          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1, G_2 \,\in\,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-tuple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big(G_1, G_2, \cdots, G_n\big)
            of groups, what is traditionally called their
            %strong free product
            and denoted
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_1 \star G_2
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\in
                  \\;
                  Grp
          %p or generally
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\star_i G_i
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  G_1 \star G_2 \star \cdots \star G_n
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\in
                  \\;
                  Grp
          %p
            is really their
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Grp
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\star_i G_i \;\simeq\; \amalg_i G_i
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\in
                  \\;
                  Grp
                  \\,.
          %p
            (Compare the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} dual notion
            of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+of+groups"}> direct product of groups
            ”, which are really
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            of groups.)
          %p
            Informally, the “free product” is the group whose elements are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} freely generated
            form those of the
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i
          %p
            More generally, if each of the given groups is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota_i \,\colon\, A \longrightarrow G_i
          %p
            from a fixed group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \,\in\, Grp
          %blockquote
            %p
              (often taken to be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
              = succeed "-inclusions" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow G_i
              and reducing to the previous situation when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = 1
              is the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial group
          %p
            then what is traditionally called their
            %strong amalgamated free product
            (or similar), and denoted
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_1 \star_A G_2
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\in
                  \\;
                  Grp
          %p or generally
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⋆
                        %mi i
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi A
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{A}{\star_i} G_i
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  G_1 \star_A G_2 \star_A \cdots \star_A G_n
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\in
                  \\;
                  Grp
          %p
            is the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_1 \star_A G_2
                  \\;\;
                  \\simeq
                  \\;\;
                  G_1 \overset{A}{\amalg} G_2
                  \\;\;
                  \\in
                  \\;
                  Grp
          %p
            (or generally the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                receives
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_i
                from the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i
                such that their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precompositions"} precompositions
                with the respective
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_i
                all agree,
            %li
              %p
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal with this property
                in that for any other group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                receiving such homomorphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
                these factor through the respective
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_i
                via a single and unique comparison homomorphism, shown as a dashed arrow in the following diagram:
          %svg{:height => "107.292pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 193.529 107.292", :width => "193.529pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
            %defs
              %g
                %symbol{:id => "3zMC_sFj3Qooly5QU_pO6yorcJo=-glyph0-0", :overflow => "visible"}
                  %path{:d => "", :style => "stroke:none;"}
