          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+product"} free product
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              copies of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+group+of+integers"} additive group of integers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi S
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F(S) \;\simeq\; \star_S \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              An abstract way to understand this elementary fact is to notice that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free construction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(G)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ⇄
                    %mi Grp
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \,\colon\,Set \rightleftarrows Grp \,\colon\, U
                    \\,.
            %p But since
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints+preserve+colimits"} left adjoints preserve colimits
                  and hence in particular
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+colimit"} preserve
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              %li
                %p
                  every set is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  of copies of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \,\in\,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                  indexed by its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
                  is the additive group of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %p we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ≃
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %munder
                            %mo ⊔
                            %mrow
                              %mi s
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi S
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ≃
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %mrow
                              %mi s
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi S
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ≃
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %mrow
                              %mi s
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi S
                          %mi ℤ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ≃
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %munder
                            %mo ⋆
                            %mrow
                              %mi s
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi S
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    F(S)
                    \\\
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    F\Big(\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} \ast\Big)
                    \\\
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\coprod} F(\ast)
                    \\\
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\coprod} \mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\star} \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
                    \\end{array}
            %p
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#Presentation Presentation
          %p
            If all the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i
            have
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+presentations"} group presentations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star_i G_i
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+presentation"} group presentation
            as follows:
          %p
            Assume
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i = \langle S_i|R_i\rangle = F_i/N_i
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i=\langle S_i\rangle
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_i
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_i\subset F_i
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i
                generated by the subset
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_i\subset F_i
          %p then the free product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⟨
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\star_i G_i
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\left\langle
                  \\coprod_i S_i | \coprod_i R_i
                  \\right\rangle
                  \\;=\;
                  (\star_i F_i)/\langle\cup_i N_i\rangle
          %p
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+presentation"} presented
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+unions"} disjoint unions
            of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_i
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_i
          %p
            (As with anything satisfying a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %h3#existence Existence
          %p Free products of groups always exist.
          %p
            With the
            %a{:href => "#Presentation"} above
            discussion of presentations this follows from the fact that any group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i
            has a presentation: we can always take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_i
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+set"} underlying set
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i
            and take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_i
            to be the set of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/words"} words
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i
            that become
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i
          %p
            The value of the more general construction above is that one often has much smaller
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_i
            to work with. Even if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_i
            is infinite, the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_i
            might be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            (in the strictest sense), making this part of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+mathematics"} finite mathematics
            and directly subject to the methods of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+group+theory"} combinatorial group theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amalgamation"} amalgamation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+of+groups"} direct product of groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product+group"} semidirect product group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+product+of+groups"} central product of groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higman-Neumann-Neumann+extension"} Higman-Neumann-Neumann extension
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of amalgamated free products of groups is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Otto+Schreier"}> Otto Schreier
              , §1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Die Untergruppen der freien Gruppen
              %strong 5
              (1927) 161–183 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02952517"}> doi:10.1007/BF02952517
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            where it is discussed (though not under any name) complete with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of what today we recognize as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            (long before this
            = succeed "-notion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          %p The actual terminology “amalgamated free product” seems to be due to:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hanna+Neumann"}> Hanna Neumann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Free Products with Amalgamated Subgroups
                %strong 71
                3 (1949) 491-540 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2372346"}> jstor:2372346
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B.+Hanna+Neumann"}> B. Hanna Neumann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Essay on Free Products of Groups with Amalgamations
                %strong 246
                919 (1954) 503-554 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/91573"}> jstor:91573
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Textbook accounts of free products of groups:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Knapp"}> Anthony Knapp
              , Section VII.3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Basic Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4529-8"} doi:10.1007/978-0-8176-4529-8
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~aknapp/download/b2-alg-clickable.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Expository review in the generality of amalgamated free products and making explicit their nature as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
          %ul
            %li
              Abhay Chandel,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Free groups and amalgamated product
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://home.iiserb.ac.in/~kashyap/Group/thesis_abhay.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Chandel-AmalgamatedProducts.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eom"}> eom
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Amalgam_of_groups"} Amalgam of groups
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of amalgamated from products:
          %ul
            %li
              A. Karrass, D. Solitar,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The subgroups of a free product of two groups with an amalgamated subgroup
              %strong 150
              1 (1970) 227-255 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1995492"}> doi:10.2307/1995492
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
